  questionText: Plant population density can be studied by various methods. The quadrat
    method helps in calculating
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: Plant population density can be studied by various methods. The
    quadrat method helps in calculating the number of individuals of each species
    with inexpensive equipment and easy fieldwork. The results from sampled quadrats
    can thus be extrapolated to the entire given field of vegetation.
  options:
